        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: protect hasTailscaleFunnelRouteForPort from unhandled JSON parse errors",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- The `JSON.parse()` call in `hasTailscaleFunnelRouteForPort` was outside the `try/catch` block after a successful `tailscale funnel status --json` exec\n- If the command returns malformed non-JSON output (corrupted state, version mismatch, etc.), the `SyntaxError` would propagate as an unhandled exception through the tailscale serve startup path\n- Moved `parsePossiblyNoisyJsonObject` into the existing `try/catch` so it degrades gracefully to `false`, consistent with other call sites (`getTailnetHostname`, `lookupTailscaleWhois`)\n- Updated test expectation from `rejects.toThrow(SyntaxError)` to `resolves.toBe(false)` to match the new graceful-degradation contract\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n### Behavior or issue addressed\nWhen `tailscale funnel status --json` succeeds (exit code 0) but returns malformed output, `hasTailscaleFunnelRouteForPort` throws an unhandled SyntaxError instead of returning `false`.\n\n### Real environment tested\nLinux x64, Node 24, unit tests with mocked exec output.\n\n### Exact steps or command run after this patch\n```\npnpm test src/infra/tailscale.test.ts\n```\n\n### Evidence after fix\n```\nTest Files  1 passed (1)\n     Tests  30 passed (30)\n```\n\n### Observed result after fix\n- Malformed JSON output → returns `false` instead of throwing\n- Noisy JSON output with warnings → still parsed correctly by `parsePossiblyNoisyJsonObject` → correct route check\n- Happy path unchanged\n- Callers that previously relied on the thrown SyntaxError now see a clean `false`\n\n### What was not tested\nLive Tailscale CLI integration (uses mocked exec).\n\n## Tests and validation\n\n- `pnpm test src/infra/tailscale.test.ts` — 30/30 pass\n- `pnpm build` — passes\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- [ ] Changes user-facing behavior\n- [ ] Changes configuration surface\n- [x] Changes error handling — degrades a previously-thrown SyntaxError to a graceful `false` return\n- [ ] Changes authentication/authorization behavior\n- [ ] Changes plugin or provider contract",
